From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spike <spike@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:23:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wasm(cargo): [patch.crates-io] vendored async-imap and
 astral-tokio-tar

Both pull mio/net on wasm32 otherwise. The vendored copies live in
docs/research/wasm-patches/support/vendor-crates/.

NOTE: [patch.crates-io] applies to native too. Vendored astral-tokio-tar
is rebased onto stock 0.6.4 (Day 11; rustix 1.0, 32-bit nanosecond fix
kept) and pinned =0.6.4. 2.63 refresh (#112): core/ now declares 0.7.0,
so the pin downgrades only the opt-in wasm copy; production core/ stays
stock. Vendored async-imap rebased onto 0.12.0 (same 2-hunk wasm delta:
drop tokio "net", wasmtimer IDLE timeout).

WASM-CORE: prototype 0001/0003 (MPL idea).
---
 Cargo.toml | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index b4ecafb..717103a 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@ tokio-io-timeout = "1.2.1"
 tokio = { package = "velta-tokio-wasm", path = "../crates/velta-tokio-wasm" }
 tokio-util = { workspace = true }
 # tar via vendored fork that routes through the shim (see [patch.crates-io])
-astral-tokio-tar = { version = "0.7.0", default-features = false }
+astral-tokio-tar = { version = "=0.6.4", default-features = false }
 
 toml = "0.9"
 url = "2"
@@ -238,3 +238,9 @@ vendored = [
 
 [lints.rust]
 unexpected_cfgs = { level = "warn", check-cfg = ['cfg(fuzzing)'] }
+
+[patch.crates-io]
+# drops unused tokio/net (breaks wasm32)
+async-imap = { path = "../vendor-crates/async-imap" }
+# routes tokio through velta-tokio-wasm so tar works on wasm32
+astral-tokio-tar = { path = "../vendor-crates/astral-tokio-tar" }
-- 
2.43.0

